    |
 22 | 		return shelf.items
    |   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    |
    = note: `shelf` belongs to whoever lent it (a parameter without `keep`, a `for` over a list, a `let` over a place), and `shelf.items` is a `Vec[Item]`. Giving it away would take a piece out of something this function doesn't own.
    = help: Write `shelf.items.clone()` for a copy. A result that is a view of a parameter on every way out is handed back as it is, with no mark.
